@startuml
title Daily knowledge-base update

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Author" as author
folder "Task2/knowledge_base\nMarkdown files" as source
component "cron\ndaily at 06:00" as cron
component "app.update_index\nlock + retry (3 attempts)" as updater
component "SHA-256 change detector" as detector
component "RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter\n500 tokens / 50 overlap" as chunker
component "Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B\n512 dimensions, normalized" as embedder
database "SQLite\ndocuments, chunks, metadata" as sqlite
database "FAISS\nIndexIDMap2(IndexFlatIP)" as faiss
database "logs\nJSONL + scheduler output" as logs
component "Index consistency validation\nSQLite IDs = FAISS IDs" as validator
component "launchd\nKeepAlive" as launchd
component "Telegram RAG bot" as bot

author --> source : add / edit / delete .md
cron --> updater : start once a day
updater --> updater : acquire non-blocking file lock
updater --> detector : scan files
source --> detector : path + content
detector --> chunker : new / changed documents
chunker --> embedder : chunks
embedder --> sqlite : text + metadata + vectors
sqlite --> faiss : rebuild derived index
updater --> validator : after transaction commit
sqlite --> validator
faiss --> validator
updater --> logs : started / retry / completed / failed
validator --> updater : counts + size or error
updater --> launchd : kickstart only if index changed
launchd --> bot : start and keep alive
bot --> sqlite : resolve chunk metadata
bot --> faiss : retrieve vectors

note right of updater
  Unchanged documents are not embedded.
  Missing files are removed from the index.
  A no-op run does not rewrite FAISS
  and does not restart the bot.
end note

note bottom of cron
  crontab.example is prepared,
  but intentionally not installed yet.
end note
@enduml
